---
// Why these exist (brief 4.4): editorial measure, the README origin stories
// in the house voice, one pull-quote moment. No invented claims: both stories
// come from the Panel Profiles and Color Timer Clock READMEs.
import Eyebrow from '../../ui/Eyebrow.astro';
import Reveal from '../../ui/Reveal.astro';
---

<section class="why" aria-label="Why these exist">
  <div class="why__inner">
    <Eyebrow label="Why these exist" />
    <Reveal as="div" class="why__body">
      <p>
        Cinnamon usually remembers your panels. It forgets them in one specific
        place: a multi-head VM where the second display shows up after Cinnamon
        has already started. You reboot, the second panel and its applets are
        gone, and you rebuild them by hand. Every reboot. Panel Profiles grew
        out of that loop: set the panels up once, save the layout as a named
        profile, restore it with one click.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="why__pull">
        The color is not decoration. It is the signal.
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        Color Timer Clock came from wanting the state of things readable from
        across the room. The clock shows when AI providers run their
        low-traffic discounts. The timer counts down to credit resets. The
        chronometer runs sprints: green for the first half hour, amber sliding
        to red over the next hour and a half, blue once two hours are up. Blue
        means take a break.
      </p>
      <p>
        Five tools later the pattern holds: put the information on the desktop,
        make it legible at a glance, then stay out of the way.
      </p>
    </Reveal>
  </div>
</section>
